# How to cite valvur. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; prepare_release.py
# moves the version and the date with each release (R39.3).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use valvur in research or an evaluation, please cite it as below."
title: "valvur: offline security scanning for AI-generated code"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "MaverickHQ"
version: "1.5.0"
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/MaverickHQ/valvur"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/valvur/"
abstract: >-
  valvur is a local-first, fully offline security scanner for AI-generated code. It runs
  seven open-source scanners in one container with no network interface, adds checks for
  hallucinated and malicious dependencies and for poisoned agent configuration, ranks
  findings by real-world exploitation, and writes an agent-readable report into the
  project. Its detection is measured by a Score of eight tracks, re-run on every phase.
keywords:
  - security
  - static analysis
  - software supply chain
  - AI-generated code
  - Model Context Protocol
  - offline
